✅ Do's: Responsible Social Media Habits
·	Think before you post: Consider if the content represents your best self and if it is something you would want a future employer or university administrator to see.
·	Regularly audit privacy settings: Check your privacy settings on all platforms to ensure only trusted friends and family can see your posts.
·	Showcase your professional brand: Use platforms like LinkedIn to highlight your skills, achievements, hobbies, and relevant projects.
·	Google yourself periodically: Perform a search of your name to see what information is publicly available, and delete anything inappropriate.
·	Verify information before sharing: Check the reliability of articles or news to avoid spreading misinformation.
·	Get consent for photos: Always ask friends or family before posting pictures of them, especially in private settings.

❌ Don'ts: Risky Social Media Habits
·	Don’t post illegal or inappropriate activities: Never post photos or statuses related to drugs, violence, underage drinking, or stealing.
·	Don’t share sensitive personal information: Avoid posting your home address, phone number, class schedule, or specific locations in real-time.
·	Don’t badmouth peers or professors: Do not use social media to vent frustrations about teachers, colleagues, or your university, as this shows a lack of maturity.
·	Don’t engage in online fights: Avoid engaging with trolls or getting into heated, public arguments, as these can ruin your reputation.
·	Don’t trust that "Private" means private: Remember that anything posted can be screenshotted and shared, even in "private" groups or disappearing stories.
·	Don’t accept requests from strangers: Be cautious of friend requests from people you do not personally know, as they could be fake profiles.
